Subject: [PATCH] ata: ahci_brcmstb: wait after releasing PHY reset

Share the existing VU Duo 4K Lite PHY reset delay with the GigaBlue Quad
4K Pro, which uses the same BCM7252S vendor kernel. Allow the PHY digital
logic to settle after releasing reset before continuing initialization.

Keep this delay in the PHY initialization path, not the I/O path.
Include linux/delay.h explicitly instead of relying on indirect includes.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [vendor kernel PHY reset workaround]
---
 drivers/ata/ahci_brcmstb.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/ata/ahci_brcmstb.c b/drivers/ata/ahci_brcmstb.c
--- a/drivers/ata/ahci_brcmstb.c
+++ b/drivers/ata/ahci_brcmstb.c
@@ -16,6 +16,7 @@
 
 #include <linux/ahci_platform.h>
 #include <linux/compiler.h>
+#include <linux/delay.h>
 #include <linux/device.h>
 #include <linux/init.h>
 #include <linux/interrupt.h>
@@ -175,6 +176,9 @@
 	reg &= ~SATA_TOP_CTRL_2_PHY_GLOBAL_RESET;
 	brcm_sata_writereg(reg, p);
 	(void)brcm_sata_readreg(p);
+
+	/* Wait for stabilization after releasing PHY reset */
+	udelay(20);
 }
 
 static void brcm_sata_phy_disable(struct brcm_ahci_priv *priv, int port)
